---
<header class="page-header wrap-narrow">
  <h1 class="page-title">Write for The AI Legal Review</h1>
</header>

<div class="prose wrap-narrow">
  <p class="lede">Students and other invited contributors can submit work concerning artificial intelligence and the law. We welcome essays, analysis and commentary that make a clear, well-supported argument.</p>

  <h2>Areas of interest</h2>
  <ul class="topic-grid">
    <li>Legal AI</li>
    <li>AI regulation</li>
    <li>Access to justice</li>
    <li>Legal technology</li>
    <li>AI and the courts</li>
    <li>Professional responsibility</li>
    <li>The future of legal practice</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These are starting points rather than limits. If your work sits elsewhere at the intersection of AI and law, we would still like to hear about it.</p>

  <h2>What we look for</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>An argument, not just a summary of developments.</li>
    <li>Accurate use of legislation, case law and secondary sources, with full references.</li>
    <li>Writing that is accessible to students and practitioners alike.</li>
    <li>Original work that you are entitled to publish.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="submit-box">
    {%- if site.submissionUrl %}
    <p>Ready to submit, or have an idea you would like to discuss?</p>
    <a class="button" href="{{ site.submissionUrl }}"{% if not site.submissionUrl.startsWith("mailto:") %} rel="noopener" target="_blank"{% endif %}>Submit your work</a>
    {%- else %}
    <p>To submit work or discuss an idea, contact the Society through Instagram. A dedicated submission form is coming soon.</p>
    <a class="button" href="{{ site.instagram }}" rel="noopener" target="_blank">{% include "partials/instagram-icon.njk" %}<span>Contact the Society</span></a>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</div>
